{
 "_readme": "Renders drawn by tools/render.py from the pack's files into wiki/renders/<name>.png (File:<name>.png on the wiki). Structure: template (one, or a list stacked like a list pool element) or jigsaw (a whole structure; seed picks the layout), processors (default: those of the pool that places the template), cut (layers removed from the top; for jigsaw {pools: regex, layers}), biome (grass, foliage and water tints), ground, camera {yaw, pitch}. Entity: layers [{model, texture, emissive}] on the game's own models (a layer of tools/render/src/entity_models.json: 'zombie' is minecraft:zombie#main, 'stray#outer' an overlay), villager {type, profession, level} (the villager's texture layers, as the game stacks them), pose (tools/render/src/models.js), equipment {asset, model, slots}, camera {yaw, pitch}. width is the width the picture is drawn for, in pixels; the file is twice that (ZOOM in render.py), so it stays sharp when zoomed, and pages set the size they show it at. skip: pages (by title) and templates (template:<id>) the picture rules in wiki/STYLE.md ask for but that don't get a picture, each with the reason; python3 tools/render.py --audit lists anything neither rendered nor skipped.",
